      "filename": "Hokitika town clock. (15913511877).jpg",
      "title": "File:Hokitika town clock. (15913511877).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/50/Hokitika_town_clock._%2815913511877%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hokitika_town_clock._(15913511877).jpg",
      "width": 2400,
      "height": 1692,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC0",
      "licenseUrl": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en",
      "artist": "Bernard Spragg. NZ from Christchurch, New Zealand",
      "description": "The Hokitika town clock also serves as the South African War memorial.\nThe Westland South African War and Coronation Memorial Clock Tower was unveiled by Mrs Seddon, the Premier’s wife, in Hokitika, on 3 June 1903, in front of her husband, General Babington and his staff, and the West Coast Battalion of Volunteers, Cadets and returned troopers.\nThe clock tower commemorated the coronation of Edward VII, the dispatch of 130 Westland men to South Africa, and four troopers who lost their lives in the war.\n\nThe foundation stone was laid in February 1902 before a crowd of two thousand, in pelting rain by Premier Seddon, who performed a full Masonic ceremony as the 'Acting Grand Master representing the New Zealand Grand Lodge.'",
      "dateCreated": "2014-12-20 12:43",
